error[E0277]: `stack_encrypt::value::Uuid` is not `Orderable`: it has no order target of its own
  --> tests/ui/order_index_on_a_uuid.rs:11:13
   |
11 |     let _ = indexed::<Uuid, (), Borrowed, _>(Ore);
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ has no order target of its own
   |
   = help: the trait `Orderable` is not implemented for `stack_encrypt::value::Uuid`
   = note: name the target: `scheme.target(I64).encrypt_checked(value)`
   = note: there is no 8-bit target: an order term over 256 values reveals them, so an `i8` goes into `I16` or wider by name (`scheme.target(I16).encrypt(value)`), or into an equality index
   = note: bytes order only into a target named for them, `scheme.target(Bytes)`: no ordering operator compares bytes
   = help: the following other types implement trait `Orderable`:
             &f32
             &f64
             &i128
             &i16
             &i32
             &i64
             &jiff::civil::date::Date
             &jiff::timestamp::Timestamp
           and $N others
   = note: there are multiple different versions of crate `vitaminc_aead` in the dependency graph
   = help: you can use `cargo tree` to explore your dependency tree
   = note: required for `stack_encrypt::Ore` to implement `stack_encrypt::Index<stack_encrypt::value::Uuid>`

